<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=elevator">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Building and engineering</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elevator</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An elevator, or lift, is a machine that carries people or goods vertically between levels; the earliest known reference, by the Roman architect Vitruvius, reports that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archimedes">Archimedes</a> built one, probably in 236 BCE. The Colosseum, completed in 80 CE, had about 25 elevators powered by men for raising animals. Steam-powered elevators served mines and factories in the mid-19th century, and in 1852 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisha">Elisha</a> Otis introduced the safety elevator, which kept the cab from falling if the cable broke; the first passenger one was installed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City in 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elevator.jpg" alt="Elevator" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Another Believer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spalding_Building,_Portland,_Oregon_(2012)_-_15.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1852</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>New York</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Elisha Otis · <a href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>A safety device already featured in Gaetano Genovese’s “flying chair” at Caserta in 1845.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/steam-engine">Steam engine<span>1606</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/skyscraper">Skyscraper<span>1885</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=elevator">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
